Today's split is wrong for the long term: overlay is natural-only (forest / swamp / jungle / glacier), while tile adds mix exclusive stamps (city, mine, plantation, fort, …) with a BUILD_ADD_STD bitfield (farm / mill / irrigation). Mutual exclusion is enforced in call sites, not in the data shape. Replace that with one primary overlay per tile that describes what the tile is currently used as, natural or man-made, plus a payload whose meaning is defined by that overlay. Terrain and climate stay orthogonal; they never stand in for occupancy. Also, some things that have been referred to as an overlay will be referred to as attributes going forward; the clearest example of this is rivers. Attributes remain orthogonal to terrain, climate, resources, and overlays, but may serve as a requirement for some improvements. What improvements belong under what overlays is completely determined by game data. 

