Each overlay maps to a fixed improvement vocabulary packed into a u16 (or similar). Some overlays have none; some have a few bits; some have more. Under farm we have things like irrigation, water mill, wind mill, dikes, and similar farm-side works — not peer overlays. Forest (and other natural/man-made uses with upgrades) get their own bit lists the same way. Map gen must emit only valid natural overlays for virgin tiles; game data / runtime helpers should reject illegal overlay transitions and illegal bits for the active overlay so exclusivity stays structural. With this design, it would be entirely fine to have a water mill both under forest and farm. One of the key virtues is it becomes crystal clear what things are mutually exclusive, and the AI choice gets reduced to picking the desired overlay. 

